From 724475a94ded441710d3740c39bc0106990996c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Patch Verification <codex@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:06:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feature: Resume available parents when V2 subagents finish

Red: just test -p codex-app-server -E test(app_server_resumes_parent_after_background_child_finishes) on rust-v0.160.0 does not start the parent when its child completes.
Green: production core requests verify idle resumption, ordinary conversation, active-turn delivery, failure, child/parent interruption, missing parent, opt-out, multiple children and follow-up identity. The combined maintained gate passes all 29 cases.

Scope: live-process best-effort delivery; no restart replay, task UI, or Monitor support.

Schema prerequisite: issue-34776/avoid-slow-agent-switching-and-resume.patch and preceding release-queue patches. Runtime behavior is unchanged by this schema-context rebase.

Catalog compatibility red: full maintained just test fails scenario catalog snapshots after completion guidance changes, and board-only scenarios observe independent automatic child completion.
Catalog compatibility green: just test -E "package(codex-core) & test(suite::scenarios::)" passes with catalog fingerprints regenerated for the new guidance and board/guardian explicit-turn fixtures explicitly disabling independent child completion. Snapshot updates preserve all content except catalog hashes and retain existing metadata.

Additional rust-v0.160.0 explicit-turn fixture compatibility:
The residency test uses explicit parent turns. The authorization fixture
injects parent history after waiting for child completion. Disable independent
completion callbacks in those fixtures so their existing contracts remain
isolated from the background-parent feature. Production behavior is unchanged.

RED: maintained affected-package run reports the residency timeout and
authorization ordering failures (final-emitted-packages.log, exit100).
GREEN: maintained focused compatibility run, 41/41 passed, exit0; includes
four residency variants, authorization variants, daemon and help fixtures.

Additional explicit-turn fixture isolation: access-program inheritance, role
service tiers, cold-root resume and model-specific tool descriptions disable
independent background callbacks in their sequence-only mocks. Dedicated
background-parent tests retain default-on behavior. No runtime change.

RED: fixture-final-workspace.log records seven affected failures (exit100).
GREEN: maintained just test focused callback-fixture-focused.log passes 7/7
cases, exit0, using the same emitted release queue with these fixture controls.

Attribution fixture red: the final emitted full suite records three starts
rather than two in child_turn_start_preserves_root_attribution. This
two-turn attribution control opts out of independent completion, while
dedicated background-parent checks retain the enabled feature.
GREEN: maintained just test -p codex-core -p codex-code-mode-host
-p codex-rmcp-client -E "test(child_turn_start_preserves_root_attribution) |
test(background_subagent_)" passes 18/18, exit0. Maintained repository
checks including just fmt-check also pass. Fresh emitted verification is pending.
